<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $512 mln August 28 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $512 mln August 28 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the seven major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $512 million to $40.549 billion in the week ended August 28, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $506 million to $40.784 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $1.888 billion to $376.963 billion.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
